"use strict";(self.webpackChunkow_ui=self.webpackChunkow_ui||[]).push([[9166],{90674:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"/2025/03/25/march-meeting","metadata":{"permalink":"/entrepreneurship-blog/2025/03/25/march-meeting","source":"@site/entrepreneurship-blog/2025-03-25-march-meeting.md","title":"Second Month Meeting Collection","description":"Entering the second month of entrepreneurship, intensively collecting data","date":"2025-03-25T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"entrepreneurship","permalink":"/entrepreneurship-blog/tags/entrepreneurship"},{"inline":true,"label":"startup meetings","permalink":"/entrepreneurship-blog/tags/startup-meetings"}],"readingTime":0.885,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Lucy","title":"Co-Founder of LZpreneur","url":"https://github.com/sad-ai-online","imageURL":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74943742?v=4","key":"lucy","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"date":"2025-03-25T00:00:00.000Z","title":"Second Month Meeting Collection","authors":["lucy"],"tags":["entrepreneurship","startup meetings"]},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"\ud83e\udd1d First Month Meeting Collection","permalink":"/entrepreneurship-blog/2025/02/28/feb-meeting"}},"content":"Entering the second month of entrepreneurship, intensively collecting data\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## 20250311\\n\\nDiscussed:\\n\\n- Tasks to complete for the week\'s Sprint\\n- Review survey collection status\\n- MVP feature brainstorming discussion\\n- Discussion on development technology framework scope\\n\\nThis day\'s meeting reviewed user survey content, brainstorming with wild creativity, discussing what users **need most**.\\n\\nLooking at survey feedback, most mentioned **lack of standardized formats**, **not knowing how to write**, **requirements easily misunderstood**, etc.\\n\\nThis made us think about our product\'s goal, which is:\\n\\n> Improve document readability!\\n\\n**Not only easy for authors to write, but also easy for readers to read** - this is the direction we want to take our product.\\n\\nWe also thought about how there are many tools, and everyone excels at different ones. The most important thing is **communication ability**.\\n\\nWhether it\'s verbal expression, written communication, or even body language, all are part of communication.\\n\\nWhat we want to do is:\\n\\n> Enable authors to write as smoothly as flowing water, while ensuring content readability gives readers a comfortable reading experience."},{"id":"/2025/02/28/feb-meeting","metadata":{"permalink":"/entrepreneurship-blog/2025/02/28/feb-meeting","source":"@site/entrepreneurship-blog/2025-02-28-feb-meeting.md","title":"\ud83e\udd1d First Month Meeting Collection","description":"Our first entrepreneurship meeting where we quickly decided on several important matters","date":"2025-02-28T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"entrepreneurship","permalink":"/entrepreneurship-blog/tags/entrepreneurship"},{"inline":true,"label":"startup meetings","permalink":"/entrepreneurship-blog/tags/startup-meetings"}],"readingTime":3.52,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Lucy","title":"Co-Founder of LZpreneur","url":"https://github.com/sad-ai-online","imageURL":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74943742?v=4","key":"lucy","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"date":"2025-02-28T00:00:00.000Z","title":"\ud83e\udd1d First Month Meeting Collection","authors":["lucy"],"tags":["entrepreneurship","startup meetings"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Second Month Meeting Collection","permalink":"/entrepreneurship-blog/2025/03/25/march-meeting"},"nextItem":{"title":"\ud83d\udea2 All Aboard the Going Merry!","permalink":"/entrepreneurship-blog/2025/02/18/going-merry"}},"content":"Our first entrepreneurship meeting where we quickly decided on several important matters\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nLet me briefly explain our division of work and approach for the entrepreneurship journey.\\n\\n## Division of Work\\n\\n`Zane`\\nA technology enthusiast with passionate dedication and an engineer\'s soul for technology, naturally taking charge of technical architecture and planning.\\n\\nAll kinds of technical knowledge and innovations can\'t escape his knowledge exploration radar. Sometimes he plays a key role in calm analysis and judgment.\\n\\nWhen I\'m hesitant and indecisive, he boldly makes decisions and we bear the consequences together \ud83d\ude06.\\n\\n<br />\\n\\n`Lucy`\\nMainly handles any management, organization, marketing, copywriting, project management, and communication tasks. Also a frontend engineer.\\n\\nFollowing `Zane` in learning technology, I\'m more of a \\"package integrator\\" - good at using and integrating, and when encountering problems, I quickly find solutions.\\n<br />\\n\\nIf we rate technical skills from 1-10, I\'m about a 6; `Zane` is a 9.\\n\\nIf we rate management skills from 1-10, I\'m about a 9; `Zane` is a 6.\\n\\n<br />\\nThis is how we established our division of work. We each have our strengths, learning to collaborate and work together to achieve our goals. \ud83e\udd78\\n\\n`Zane` develops the main framework, while I work within that framework, taking notes while developing.\\n\\n## Meeting Approach\\n\\nWe have a fixed weekly meeting schedule, and when there are more items to discuss, we arrange additional meetings.\\n\\nEach meeting is fixed at 2-2.5 hours, with one Sprint per week.\\n\\nMeetings mainly discuss tasks to be executed that week, and we also decide on solutions for content prepared before meetings.\\n\\nWe don\'t waste any precious time, because we each have other life priorities to attend to.\\n\\nWhile entrepreneurship is certainly one of the dream list items we want to try in life, we won\'t neglect other precious people and things in our lives.\\n\\nSo our meetings are focused and concentrated - discuss, decide, reflect, and proceed with meeting priorities with swift decisiveness!\\n\\n## 20250218\\n\\nIn our first meeting, I had already organized the items to be decided beforehand, such as:\\n\\n- domain\\n- official website content\\n- product MVP features\\n- timeline planning\\n\\nWhen we both lack ideas, we\'re both the type who suffer from choice paralysis.\\n\\nThis meeting, we spent the most time **deciding on the domain name**.\\n\\nBecause our original name had already been taken, we listed several combinations,\\n\\nand considering SEO factors, we really didn\'t know which was best.\\n\\nFinding a suitable domain took about 30 minutes front and back, which was quite long, and our indecision left us feeling lost.\\n\\nSo we used the elimination method, leaving three suitable names,\\n\\n<br />\\n\\nThen! We used a **spinning wheel to decide** - whichever name the wheel landed on, we\'d buy that domain! \ud83d\ude0a\\n\\nThis saved us a lot of energy \ud83d\ude05\\n\\n<br />\\n\\nOther items were also smoothly discussed and suitable approaches were found. The lesson learned that day was:\\n\\n> When you\'re indecisive, leave it to the spinning wheel!\\n\\n## 20250225\\n\\nThis day we discussed:\\n\\n- UI Mockup\\n- Transferring the initial website to a new account\\n- Deciding on project management tools\\n- Reviewing MVP feature feasibility assessment\\n- Establishing Discord channels\\n- Tentative product logo\\n\\nSince we\'re both usually very busy - one busy caring for family and getting certifications, the other busy with exercise and life management.\\n\\nThis day\'s meeting, `Zane` very quickly handled the GitHub repo and GitHub Actions to a good point.\\n\\n<br />\\n\\nNext, we discussed whether to switch from our original `ClickUp` to `JIRA` and `Confluence` for project management.\\n\\nFinally, considering familiarity, interface readability, and cost, we decided to abandon `ClickUp`.\\n\\n> Because time is most precious to us. The most important thing is to move the project forward first.\\n\\n## 20250227\\n\\nDiscussed:\\n\\n- Tasks to complete for the week\'s Sprint\\n- Continue adjusting the product website\'s CI/CD\\n- Adjusting Discord channel naming conventions and permission settings\\n- Surveying language frameworks\\n\\nThis day\'s meeting was less than 2 hours, and we quickly listed all the items that needed to be listed clearly.\\nThen it was time for execution and completion.\\n\\n> Once a choice is made, don\'t look back wondering if it\'s right. Just make it right!"},{"id":"/2025/02/18/going-merry","metadata":{"permalink":"/entrepreneurship-blog/2025/02/18/going-merry","source":"@site/entrepreneurship-blog/2025-02-18-going-merry.md","title":"\ud83d\udea2 All Aboard the Going Merry!","description":"A simple record of our journey in planning products and project development. Let\'s dive in!","date":"2025-02-18T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"entrepreneurship","permalink":"/entrepreneurship-blog/tags/entrepreneurship"},{"inline":true,"label":"engineer entrepreneurship","permalink":"/entrepreneurship-blog/tags/engineer-entrepreneurship"}],"readingTime":1.675,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Lucy","title":"Co-Founder of LZpreneur","url":"https://github.com/sad-ai-online","imageURL":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74943742?v=4","key":"lucy","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"date":"2025-02-18T00:00:00.000Z","title":"\ud83d\udea2 All Aboard the Going Merry!","authors":["lucy"],"tags":["entrepreneurship","engineer entrepreneurship"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"\ud83e\udd1d First Month Meeting Collection","permalink":"/entrepreneurship-blog/2025/02/28/feb-meeting"}},"content":"A simple record of our journey in planning products and project development. Let\'s dive in!\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## The Beginning\\n\\nEntrepreneurship was always something far from our reality.\\n\\nBecause the skill set required for entrepreneurship is both broad and deep - not just programming, but also understanding marketing.\\n\\nWe\'ve always felt intimidated by knowledge outside the technical domain.\\n\\n<br />\\n\\nHowever, after starting to explore marketing knowledge in 2020, we discovered that the ideas and things around us in daily life are interconnected.\\n\\n> Turns out, entrepreneurship seems quite interesting!\\n\\n<br />\\n\\nOver these years, besides technical knowledge and hands-on experience, we\'ve also accumulated marketing knowledge and experimentation.\\n\\nStep by step, we\'ve built up to where we are now, and we\'re eager to try \\"entrepreneurship.\\"\\n\\nWe\'re not sure what we\'ll encounter on this entrepreneurship journey, but I\'m certain it won\'t be simple.\\n\\n## The Catalyst\\n\\nOne day, Jerry shared a book:\\n\\n> What got you here, won\'t get you there.\\n\\nIt mentioned that current success can be achieved through method A.\\nBut to achieve a different kind of success, method A might not have the same effect.\\n\\nTo gain different experiences, you need to try a different approach to make it possible.\\n\\nSo why not \\"start a business\\"! Let\'s see what interesting people and things we encounter along the way.\\n\\n<br />\\n\\nSo we thought about what problems are waiting for us to solve, and what we have the capability to handle.\\n\\nCoincidentally, we often encounter **unclear requirements and poorly written documentation** at work.\\n\\nThis often wastes development time, increases communication costs, delays project timelines, and overall creates a poor development experience.\\n\\nCan we solve this? We think so! ~~Our internal dialogue was basically \\"Are we serious? Should we go for it?\\"~~\\n\\n<br />\\n\\nSo let\'s give it a try! That\'s how **LZpreneur** was born.\\n\\nMoving forward, we\'ll record our monthly meeting content and entrepreneurship decisions.\\n\\nWe want to share this with engineers who want to start businesses. Are you ready?\\n\\nLet\'s set sail!"}]}}')}}]);